  {
   "name": "soft control, no skull plate",
   "why": "control for the refine pass. Round 21's combined variant read the same as the baseline and its front showed a flat boxed plate between the eye and the cup (about .036 wide, the same as the skull_ramp .04 it set) plus one flat white slab for the tuft. This keeps the cached soft rear (skin blend .012, strip smoothing 6, no K root shift, dome blur 10: the only rear edit that scored well) and the floater-safe soft front, but sets skull_ramp to .012 so the cup meets the skull in a fillet instead of a plate; every other front lever stays at the starter, so later variants read against it (R03.5, R03.7)",
